James Rising received an email from Hannah Rogers, an undergraduate in economics with a focus on climate economics and coastal impacts. She expressed admiration for his research and inquired about graduate mentorship opportunities for the 2027-2028 academic year, attaching her CV. James requested assistance in drafting a professional response. The resulting email acknowledged Hannah’s interest, indicated that he is not taking new students at the moment, and suggested she check back later in the year. He also proposed a Zoom meeting to discuss her background and interests further, providing a scheduling link for convenience.
